For Type 1 regulated activity, the licensee shall not conduct business other than: &ndash;

(a) communicating offers to effect dealings in securities to other intermediaries in the names of the persons from whom those offers are received;
(b) introducing persons to other intermediaries, in order that such persons may: -
(i) effect dealings in securities; or 
(ii) make offers to deal in securities; and
(c) dealing in collective investment schemes. The terms &ldquo;collective investment scheme&rdquo; and &ldquo;dealing&rdquo; are as defined under the Securities and Futures Ordinance.

For Type 1 regulated activity, the licensee shall not engage in dealing activities other than &ndash; 
(a) underwriting, sub-underwriting and placing of securities; 
(b) communicating offers to effect dealings in securities to other intermediaries, for the persons from whom those offers are received; and
(c) introducing persons to other intermediaries, in order that such persons may:
(i) effect dealings in securities; or
(ii) make offers to deal in securities.

For Type 3 regulated activity, the licensee shall not conduct business other than &ndash;
(a) Introducing persons to Brown Brothers Harriman & Co in order that they may:
(i) effect trading in leveraged foreign exchange contracts in the United States of America; or
(ii) make offers to trade in leveraged foreign exchange contracts in the United States of America; 
(b) Communicating offers to effect leveraged foreign exchange trading to Brown Brothers Harriman & Co in the names of the persons from whom those offers are received; and
(c) Negotiating leveraged foreign exchange contracts with persons on behalf of Brown Brothers Harriman & Co.

For Type 7 regulated activity, the licensee shall:
(1) have appropriate arrangements in place that enable it to:
(a) monitor transactions undertaken on the ETS to identify suspected breaches of any rules relating to fair and orderly trading on the ETS and conduct that may constitute market abuse; 
(b) report to the Commission suspected material breaches of its rules relating to fair and orderly trading on the ETS or suspected market abuse; and 
(c) upon request from the Commission, supply relevant information to the Commission as soon as practicable regarding any suspected breaches or suspected market abuse and provide full assistance to the Commission in inquiring into or investigating the suspected breaches or suspected market abuse.
(2) notify the Commission on any material changes to the matters specified below, prior to the changes taking effect:
(a) corporate structure and governance arrangement;
(b) business plan/operations;
(c) the ETS (including changes in trading rules, operator of the system, hardware, software, and other technology);
(d) its contractual responsibilities for clients of the ETS; and
(e) criteria for approval or disapproval of clients of the ETS.
(3) put in place appropriate business continuity plans and disaster recovery programmes for its operations and the ETS and notify the Commission of any material changes to the plans or programmes.

